note bottom of Timer
  Client-side countdown. On expiry the
  waiting client calls Server.claimTimeout();
  the server re-checks turnStartedAt /
  disconnectedAt (turnTimerExpired,
  gracePeriodElapsed in 6.2 and 6.3) and
  returns false if not yet up (try again).
end note
note bottom of NetworkHandler
  Broadcasts come from a database trigger on
  games, so broadcast() is not used. Each one
  goes to onBroadcast (fast path), then
  resync() refetches getMyState for onState
  (the truth), also after every reconnect.
  PrivatePayload (scan result, ability offer,
  or the opponent's abilityUsed notice) goes
  to the owner's own channel.
  The opponent's presence leave calls
  reportDisconnect(); a waiting host calls
  keepLobbyOpen() every 10 s. ServerCalls
  are those server actions (fakes in tests).
end note
note bottom of AudioManager
  Optional. Does nothing while
  AUDIO_ENABLED is false.
end note
legend bottom right
  Grey dashed boxes are classes detailed in another figure.
endlegend
